We[ quickly] jumped into[ the] car[ and] drove round to where they’d been spotted. We found[ them] quickly, and I started towards[ them with my] trust[y] bucket. Usually they[ would] run towards me, but not today.[ They were rather] spooked. I suspect that they’[d met a] few people out walking[ their] dogs and this had put them in rather a fluster. Instead we did the human sheep dog thing,[ and] soon had[ them] heading in the right direction.[ They]’[d clearly had] enough of[ an] adventure, and were happy[ to] be heading home. I stayed on after them, both to make sure they didn’[t] change their minds, and also to see where they’d got out, and within a few minutes they[ were all] safely back in their field.
